Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: explorer: only set shell window for shell-enabled desktops
 The auto-spawned explorer.exe /desktop instance unconditionally called
 SetShellWindow() on a visible window station, claiming the shell role
 before the real shell (ReactOS explorer) starts. ReactOS explorer checks
 GetShellWindow() at startup and exits immediately when a shell window
 already exists, so the CDEX session ended up with no taskbar or desktop.
 Gate the SetShellWindow() call behind enable_shell, which is only true
 for named desktops with shell integration enabled (the magic "shell"
 desktop or an explicit EnableShell registry setting), so the lazily
 spawned /desktop instance keeps hosting the desktop window and display
 driver without stealing the shell role.
Last-Modified: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 18:40:00 +0300

--- a/src/programs/explorer/desktop.c
+++ b/src/programs/explorer/desktop.c
@@ -1320,8 +1320,11 @@
     shellwindows_init();
 
     /* Ideally we would set the window of an IShellView here, but we never
-       actually create one, so the desktop window itself will have to do. */
-    set_shell_window( hwnd );
+       actually create one, so the desktop window itself will have to do.
+       Only claim the shell window when shell integration is enabled for this
+       desktop: the auto-spawned /desktop instance must not steal the shell
+       role from a real shell such as the ReactOS explorer. */
+    if (enable_shell) set_shell_window( hwnd );
 
     /* run the desktop message loop */
     if (hwnd)
